WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.230
Old-style sun cream did its job,

2
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:06.010
but it left a thick white
film all over your skin.

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.530
Modern sun cream can use
the same kind of substance,

4
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.550
and still block harmful
ultraviolet light.

5
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.550
But it rubs in clear.

6
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.090
Nothing about the substance
has changed except one thing:

7
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.410
the size of its particles.

8
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:23.310
They are now so small that each
one is only a few hundred atoms

9
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.530
across.

10
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.210
So why should size matter?

11
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.220
In this mission, you'll see how
small a nanoparticle really is.

12
00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:34.810
You'll work out how surface
area compares with volume as

13
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.430
particles shrink, and weigh up
the benefits and risks of using

14
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:38.810
them.

15
00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:44.190
Your mission: explain why size
changes how a substance behaves.
